            "Trigonal system. Elongated, striated prisms with a rounded triangular cross-section. No distinct cleavage; conchoidal to uneven fracture. Hardness 7 to 7.5; specific gravity 3.01 to 3.06; vitreous lustre; refractive index 1.62 to 1.64; birefringence 0.018 to 0.020 (uniaxial negative). Distinct pleochroism, light pink and deep pink. Fluid inclusions and growth fractures are common in saturated stones. Pyroelectric. It is sometimes heated or irradiated to intensify or lighten the colour; these treatments are generally stable.",
            "Brazil: Minas Gerais (Cruzeiro, Barra de Salinas), a major source. United States: California, the Pala district and the Himalaya mine at Mesa Grande, famous in the late 19th century thanks to purchases by Empress Dowager Cixi; Maine (Newry). Mozambique, Nigeria, Madagascar, Afghanistan and Namibia complete the production.",
            "A stone of love, gentleness and compassion, said to soothe sorrow and open the heart. It is one of the October birthstones. It is associated with the heart chakra and the sign of Libra. Cleansing under lukewarm water; recharging in moonlight or gentle sunlight."
        ),
